    "productSpecificRisks": [
      {
        "text": "Whilst the transactions are pending, there could be movements within the stock-market; that is to say that the stock-market could rise or fall in value. If the market rises in value between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new (funds), you could be financially disadvantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new fund could be greater.",
        "topic": "TransitionRisk",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "documentId": "Suitability Report Test 1.pdf",
          "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Conversely, if there is a fall in the market between the date of realising your existing funds and the purchase of your new funds, you could be financially advantaged insofar as the cost of buying your new funds could be lower.",
        "topic": "TransitionRisk",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "documentId": "Suitability Report Test 1.pdf",
          "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Should you require access to these funds in the future it will usually take 10-15 working days for administration, disinvestment and banking processes to complete.",
        "topic": "AccessibilityDelay",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "documentId": "Suitability Report Test 1.pdf",
          "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "There is no guarantee the return on the new investment will be greater than that of your existing arrangement for these funds.",
        "topic": "NoOutperformanceGuarantee",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "documentId": "Suitability Report Test 1.pdf",
          "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
          "pageNumbers": [
            8
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Other Considerations of Switching"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "A switch between pension providers does not guarantee a greater pension fund at retirement and there is no guarantee that the new provider\u0027s funds will outperform those of your existing provider.",
        "topic": "NoOutperformanceGuarantee",
        "isClientSpecific": false,
        "provenance": {
          "assertionStatus": "Stated",
          "documentId": "Suitability Report Test 1.pdf",
          "documentCategory": "I_RecommendationsAndAdvice",
          "pageNumbers": [
            12
          ],
          "sectionHeading": "Fund recommendation"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": "Pensions are currently outside of your estate for IHT purposes, however from 6 April 2027, most unused defined contribution pensions and death benefits (such as drawdown funds and uncrystallised pots) will be included in your taxable estate for IHT.",
        "topic": "InheritanceTaxChange",
        "isClientSpecific": true,
        "provenance": {
